---
/** Interface demo: hints with the script (upgraded to a text-only tooltip) and with CSS alone. */
---
<p class="muted">With the script: a text-only tooltip, placed to fit the window, read by screen readers.</p>
<div class="card card--compact"><div class="demo-row">
  <span class="hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Visits that left after one page, as a share of all visits. Lower is better.">Bounce rate</span>
  <span class="status-chip status-chip--warning hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Two of nine goals are behind schedule.">At risk</span>
  <span class="hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Prefers aligning to its end; flips if that would leave the window." data-align="end">End-aligned</span>
</div></div>
<p class="muted">With CSS alone (a page on omds.css only): drawn below, inside the page, not read by screen readers.</p>
<div class="card card--compact" data-demo="css-only"><div class="demo-row">
  <span class="hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Visits that left after one page, as a share of all visits. Lower is better.">Bounce rate</span>
  <span class="status-chip status-chip--warning hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Two of nine goals are behind schedule.">At risk</span>
  <span class="hint" tabindex="0" data-hint="Aligned to its end, for a hint near the window's right edge." data-align="end">End-aligned</span>
</div></div>
<p class="muted">Rest the pointer on one or tab to it: both open at once.</p>
